  "notes": [
    {
      "marker": "1.",
      "text": "COMM courses at 2000 and above level will be included in the calculation of Major GPA for honours classification.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "2.",
      "text": "Students may be required to take pre-requisite courses for courses under specific areas.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "3.",
      "text": "Students may take COMM courses outside of their study schemes as their Major elective courses, and the course grades will be included in the calculation of Major GPA.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "4.",
      "text": "Any students should have taken at least 36 units of SOCI courses before making official declaration to take the Journalism and Communication as their second major.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "5.",
      "text": "Students who pursue a second Major in Sociology can complete COMM1120, SOCI1001 and one Faculty Package course offered by a Programme/Department/School other than SOCI and COMM to satisfy the Faculty Package course requirements of both Major Programmes.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "6.",
      "text": "Students who pursue a second major in Sociology can be exempted from taking SOCI2003 by taking COMM2160 as the units earned can be counted towards both Major Programmes.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "7.",
      "text": "Students who pursue a second major in Sociology can be exempted from taking SOCI1002, and are required to take another SOCI course to compensate for the units to fulfill the Sociology major requirements.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "8.",
      "text": "Student must have taken or registered for at least 21 units of SOCI courses at the last term of attendance before making declaration to take Sociology as their second major.",
      "subsections": [],
      "rows": []
    }
  ],
